      "narration": "The catch here is genuinely cruel. Good habits usually pay off far in the future, while bad habits feel great right now. Our brains were built to prize the immediate reward. So you have to bridge that gap. Add a small reward you can actually feel today, something that tells your brain, right now, that this new behavior was worth repeating.",
